KZ3 patch 3006: PAD_SCRIPT v2 (gameplay test plan B1). Scripted pad input with per-event holds,
analog stick and trigger segments, a file form with comments, a raised event limit and one log line per fired
event. v1 was digital only, kept at most 32 events (pad-r12 has 47; the rest were dropped silently) and held
each 40 polls. Old "sec:mask" scripts behave exactly as before.

Grammar (PAD_SCRIPT="..." and PAD_SCRIPT_FILE=path take the same text and add up; events need not be sorted):
  script := event { sep event }        sep = ',' | space | tab | newline; '#' comments to end of line
  event  := T ':' body [ '/' SECONDS ] T = wall-clock seconds since the first pad poll (float)
  body   := MASK                       digital press, C number (0x4000 or 16384); held 40 polls,
                                       or SECONDS when '/' is given
          | LX ',' LY ',' RX ',' RY [ ',' L2 ',' R2 ]
                                       analog hold: sticks -1..1 (0 centred; LY/RY -1 = up, +1 = down),
                                       triggers 0..1 (pressure; above 0.5 the digital L2/R2 bit is set too);
                                       held SECONDS, default 1 s
Examples:  10:0x4000  (CROSS, 40 polls)   300:0x0100/3  (L2 held 3 s)   430:0,-1,0,0/10  (left stick up 10 s)
           440:0,0,1,0,0,1/2  (right stick right + R2 for 2 s)
Masks: (DIGITAL2 << 8) | DIGITAL1: SELECT 0x0001 L3 0x0002 R3 0x0004 START 0x0008 UP 0x0010 RIGHT 0x0020
DOWN 0x0040 LEFT 0x0080 L2 0x0100 R2 0x0200 L1 0x0400 R1 0x0800 TRIANGLE 0x1000 CIRCLE 0x2000 CROSS 0x4000
SQUARE 0x8000.

Events latch (fire at the first poll at or after T, a loading screen stops polling) and hold from then; digital
bits of overlapping events OR together, the latest-fired analog hold wins and the sticks return to centre after
it. Log: "[cellPad] PAD_SCRIPT: N event(s)" plus a WARNING line for dropped (> PAD_SCRIPT_MAX = 1024) or
unparsable events at start, then "[cellPad] script t=Ts press 0xMMMM for ..." / "... sticks l=(x,y) r=(x,y)
l2=.. r2=.. for ..s" per fired event, at most 20 per wall second. Host test: tools/upstream/test_pad_script_v2.py.
Upstream candidate (general: any title's headless test driving).

